{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CetKupbLzikiXzXQjDouu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Repository findings:**\n\n- ShipmentController.kt (lines 20-56): Handles POST /shipments (create), GET /shipments/{id}, GET /shipments (list)\n- Shipment.kt (lines 1-34): Data model with ShipmentStatus enum (CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)\n- ShipmentRepository.kt (lines 1-27): In-memory repository with save, existsById, findById, findAll\n- ApiExceptions.kt (lines 1-30): ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404)\n- ApiError.kt (lines 1-37): ErrorCode enum with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS\n- GlobalExceptionHandler.kt (lines 1-29): Centralized exception handler\n\n**Conventions in this repository:**\n\n- Error responses use `ApiException` subclasses that automatically convert to the error envelope\n- `ConflictException` with `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS` used for 409 conflicts\n- `ResourceNotFoundException` with `ErrorCode.SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND` used for 404 not found\n- Controllers are thin and delegate to exceptions for error signaling\n- Tests use MockMvc with jsonPath assertions\n- The pattern is: throw exception → GlobalExceptionHandler catches → ApiError envelope returned\n\n**Affected files:**\n\n1. `ApiError.kt` - Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` error code (cannot avoid: need new error type for 409 when shipment is cancelled)\n2. `ShipmentController.kt` - Add `confirm()` method with `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` (core requirement)\n3. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` - Add 4 test cases for confirm endpoint (cannot avoid: requirement demands tests)\n\n**Risks:**\n\n- Existing tests could break if the shipment model or repository changes\n- Idempotency must be preserved (retry must succeed, not fail)\n- Need to ensure status transition logic is correct\n\n**Open questions:**\n\nNone. The requirement is clear: CREATED→CONFIRMED on first confirm, no-op on already CONFIRMED, 409 on CANCELLED, 404 on not found.\n\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_CANCELLED` to ErrorCode enum. This is a new error code to distinguish \"shipment is cancelled\" (409) from \"shipment not found\" (404).\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new endpoint method:\n   ```\n   @PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")\n   fun confirm(@PathVariable shipmentId: String): Shipment\n   ```\n   Logic:\n   - Find shipment by ID; if not found, throw ResourceNotFoundException\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - If status is CREATED, copy shipment with status=CONFIRMED, save and return\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, return as-is (idempotent)\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add 4 test methods:\n   - `test_confirms_created_shipment_to_confirmed()`: Create S-1, confirm it, verify status is CONFIRMED\n   - `test_confirming_already_confirmed_succeeds()`: Create S-2, confirm twice, verify both succeed\n   - `test_confirming_cancelled_shipment_fails_with_409()`: Manually save cancelled shipment, confirm, expect 409 with SHIPMENT_CANCELLED\n   - `test_confirming_nonexistent_shipment_fails_with_404()`: Confirm S-999, expect 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Alternative*: Create a separate `ShipmentService` class to handle business logic. \n- *Why rejected*: The OrderController and existing code do not use a service layer; they handle logic directly. Keeping consistency with the existing codebase is more important, and we're constrained to not refactor unrelated files.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n1. **Confirm CREATED shipment** (200 OK):\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller finds S-1 with status=CREATED\n   - Creates new Shipment with status=CONFIRMED\n   - Saves via repository.save()\n   - Returns 200 + Shipment body\n\n2. **Confirm already CONFIRMED shipment** (200 OK):\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm\n   - Controller finds S-1 with status=CONFIRMED\n   - Returns as-is without modification\n   - Returns 200 + Shipment body (idempotent)\n\n3. **Confirm CANCELLED shipment** (409 Conflict):\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-1/confirm (where status=CANCELLED)\n   - Controller finds S-1, detects status=CANCELLED\n   - Throws ConflictException(SHIPMENT_CANCELLED, message)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 409 + ApiError envelope\n\n4. **Confirm non-existent shipment** (404 Not Found):\n   - Request: POST /shipments/S-999/confirm\n   - Controller findById returns null\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException(SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND, message)\n   - GlobalExceptionHandler catches, returns 404 + ApiError envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. Test 1: Happy path - confirm CREATED → CONFIRMED (verifies core feature)\n2. Test 2: Idempotency - confirm twice, both succeed (verifies retry safety)\n3. Test 3: Conflict - cancel then confirm fails 409 (verifies business rule)\n4. Test 4: Not found - confirm non-existent fails 404 (verifies error handling)\n\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1211,"cache_read_input_tokens":18536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1211},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"693b0b6b-30e7-4ce6-8483-8e14b0f515e4","uuid":"e8e441ac-62a2-4896-a4f0-cf514f912c5d","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:19:30.624Z","request_id":"req_011CetKuodoJ1WfGbWeaiguF"}
