tException if status is CANCELLED\n   - Idempotency: returns as-is if already CONFIRMED\n   - Persistence: saves with new status if CREATED\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** — Added 4 test methods (46 lines). Each covers one requirement:\n   - Test 1: Happy path (CREATED → CONFIRMED)\n   - Test 2: Idempotency (retry succeeds)\n   - Test 3: Business rule (cancelled rejected with 409)\n   - Test 4: Error handling (non-existent rejected with 404)\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All requirements met, all tests pass, no extra changes made.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /shipments/{shipmentId}/confirm endpoint that moves CREATED shipments to CONFIRMED, allows retry on CONFIRMED, rejects CANCELLED with 409, rejects non-existent with 404.\nChanged       ApiError.kt - Added SHIPMENT_CANCELLED error code to distinguish cancelled-shipment errors\nChanged       ShipmentController.kt - Added confirm() endpoint with logic for status transitions and error handling\nChanged       ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added 4 test cases for confirm endpoint covering happy path, idempotency, conflict, and not found scenarios\nTests         Test 1: confirms_created_shipment_to_confirmed - verifies CREATED→CONFIRMED transition and persistence\nTests         Test 2: confirming_already_confirmed_succeeds_idempotently - verifies retry safety (idempotent)\nTests         Test 3: confirming_cancelled_shipment_fails_with_409 - verifies business rule rejection\nTests         Test 4: confirming_non_existent_shipment_fails_with_404 - verifies error handling for missing resource\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/; Result: BUILD SUCCESS, 17 tests run, 0 failures\nNot done      (none - all requirements implemented and verified)\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3316,"cache_read_input_tokens":23614,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_